From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skyjet18 <57456827+skyjet18@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:28:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/49] dashdec: fix integer overflow by seeking

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0026-dashdec-fix-integer-overflow-by-seeking.patch.
Port: applied clean (offset only).
Review: av_rescale(duration, 1000, fragment_timescale) instead of the
integer-second (duration / timescale) * 1000: no overflow and no loss
of the sub-second part of the segment boundaries.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/dashdec.c b/libavformat/dashdec.c
index c6b48d66..9ebe1538 100644
--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -2652,13 +2652,13 @@ static int dash_seek(AVFormatContext *s, struct representation *pls, int64_t see
                 duration = pls->timelines[i]->starttime;
             }
             duration += pls->timelines[i]->duration;
-            if (seek_pos_msec < ((duration * 1000) /  pls->fragment_timescale)) {
+            if (seek_pos_msec < av_rescale(duration, 1000, pls->fragment_timescale)) {
                 goto set_seq_num;
             }
             for (j = 0; j < pls->timelines[i]->repeat; j++) {
                 duration += pls->timelines[i]->duration;
                 num++;
-                if (seek_pos_msec < ((duration * 1000) /  pls->fragment_timescale)) {
+                if (seek_pos_msec < av_rescale(duration, 1000, pls->fragment_timescale)) {
                     goto set_seq_num;
                 }
             }
